{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfUvVfiqpSmTMBogZWjeP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two small changes to `0.html`:\n\n1. **Stricter security policy:** It now blocks everything by default and only allows what the page actually uses: the inline styles and the inline favicon. The page doesn't load scripts or any other files, so nothing visible changes. It just protects the page if something gets injected into it later.\n2. **Less space under the title:** The header's bottom padding, the header's bottom margin and the title's own bottom margin were all adding space in the same spot, so the gap between the title and the text was too big. Now only the title's margin sets that gap.\n\nA few things I left alone because they're your call:\n- **`<meta name=\"author\">` publishes your email address**, and scrapers can harvest it for spam. I'd put your name there instead.\n- **Placeholder links:** `example.com` is still used for the canonical link and the social-preview image (`og:image`, `twitter:image`). Link previews on social sites will break until you swap in the real URLs.\n- **The footer says \"© 2026\" without a name.** Something like \"© 2026 K. Smith\" would say who owns it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":7021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1145},"output_tokens":346,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b488658-415b-4fb4-9c24-8fc38b8e2624","uuid":"f529710b-a62e-42b3-9a91-91afeb23961e","timestamp":"2026-09-28T00:53:02.610Z","request_id":"req_011CfUvVfNW3Rav3yoykjKGx"}
